"},"foregroundColor":{"opaqueColor":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.8509803921568627,"green":0.18823529411764706,"blue":0.1450980392156863}}}},"fields":"bold,fontFamily,fontSize,foregroundColor"}},{"updateTextStyle":{"objectId":"sol6k3","textRange":{"type":"FIXED_RANGE","startIndex":7,"endIndex":54},"style":{"bold":false,"fontFamily":"Roboto","fontSize":{"magnitude":9.5,"unit":"PT"},"foregroundColor":{"opaqueColor":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.37254901960784315,"green":0.38823529411764707,"blue":0.40784313725490196}}}},"fields":"bold,fontFamily,fontSize,foregroundColor"}},{"createShape":{"objectId":"sol6tn","shapeType":"TEXT_BOX","elementProperties":{"pageObjectId":"p8","size":{"width":{"magnitude":11091672,"unit":"EMU"},"height":{"magnitude":1280160,"unit":"EMU"}},"transform":{"scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"translateX":548640,"translateY":5084064,"unit":"EMU"}}}},{"insertText":{"objectId":"sol6tn","insertionIndex":0,"text":"Why A wins, and why B is not the answer despite the widest reach.  B reaches the 74% who never type anything, which is the largest behaviour in our data, and it still loses. It scores 5 on confidence because no user asked for a form; it came from us and from desk research. A wins on evidence: a controlled test in which only the date phrasing changed, plus three unprompted requests from two participants for exactly this interaction. That is a legitimate reason to go first, and B is named as the next bet rather than dropped.\nDeliberately out of this round:  the stage-5 recovery loop, which desk research rates the single biggest opportunity and we rate second. The MVP user test is designed to tell us whether that ordering is wrong.\n"}},{"updateTextStyle":{"objectId":"sol6tn","textRange":{"type":"FIXED_RANGE","startIndex":0,"endIndex":65},"style":{"bold":true,"fontFamily":"Roboto","fontSize":{"magnitude":10.5,"unit":"PT"},"foregroundColor":{"opaqueColor":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.12549019607843137,"green":0.12941176470588237,"blue":0.1411764705882353}}}},"fields":"bold,fontFamil